| Claim | Reality |
|---|---|
| 1. No first-login handle claim | `components/dashboard/username-prompt.tsx` is a **non-dismissible** dialog (no close, no outside-click, no escape) shown whenever `username` is empty, routing to `/profile`. The path exists and is mandatory. |
| 1b. `isNew` is discarded | True, and harmless. `username === null` is the same signal and already drives the prompt. Reading `isNew` would add a second source of truth for one boolean. |
| 3. Hex account id not offered | Already the "Account ID" tab in `components/deposit/deposit-address-card.tsx`, copyable, with its own QR. |
| 5. No transaction detail view | `components/transactions/transaction-list.tsx` rows are accordions exposing from / to / amount / fee / status / block index with explorer link. `getTransactionDetail` would return a record already in memory. |
| 8. Profile implies editability | It does not. `components/profile/profile-card.tsx` renders a claimed handle as static text plus a permanence note; the form exists only when unclaimed. |

## `register` vs `updateUsername` — kept `updateUsername`

`AuthService.register` and `UserService.updateUsername` run the identical
set-once claim: same validator, same reserved check, same taken check, same
`setUsername`, same permanence rejection. The only difference is `register`
also creates the user record when absent, which cannot happen in the browser
because `openBackendSession` always calls `login()` first.

Swapping would be pure churn on a production money path with no behavioural
difference, so `updateUsername` stays. `register` remains available for any
non-browser client.

