### Correction to the settings section above

`getSettings` is **not** a query. `SettingsService.getSettings` calls
`SettingsRepo.getOrCreate`, which mutates stable state, so the method is
declared `public shared` and costs a full update call. That is why the drawer
reads once per session rather than on every open, and writes on close rather
than on every toggle.

Scope is theme and language only. `notifications` is read and echoed back
unchanged — nothing in the frontend controls it. Fiat and sound stay
client-only; they are not in `SettingsPublic` and adding them would require a
stable-record migration. localStorage remains authoritative for first paint;
the canister is the cross-device sync layer.

